NNOOTTEESS
     Disabling tracing on a process should not be considered a security fea‐
     ture, as it is bypassable both by the kernel and privileged processes and
     via other system mechanisms.  As such, it should not be utilized to reli‐
     ably protect cryptographic keying material or other confidential data.

     Note that processes can trivially bypass the 'no simultaneously writable
     and executable mappings' policy by first marking some mapping as write‐
     able, writing code to it, then removing write and adding execute permis‐
     sion.  This may be legitimately required by some programs such as JIT
     compilers.

